functools.reduce
 1. reduce(operator.add, nums)                                 10
 2. reduce(lambda acc, x: acc + x, nums, 0)                    10
 3. reduce(operator.add, nums, 10)  (initial value last)       20
 4. reduce(operator.mul, nums)                                 24
 5. one name; hasattr(builtins, "reduce")                      [10, False]
 6. reduce(add, []) raises; reduce(add, [], 0); sum([])        ['TypeError', 0, 0]
 7. reduce(never, [7])  (one element: no call)                 7
 8. reduce(lambda best, w: longer of the two, words)           'banana'
 9. reduce(math.lcm, range(1, 6)), reduce(math.gcd, ...)       [60, 6]

sum is not reduce(add): floats are compensated since 3.12
10. reduce(operator.add, [0.1] * 10)                           0.9999999999999999
11. sum([0.1] * 10), math.fsum([0.1] * 10)                     [1.0, 1.0]
12. reduce(add, [1e100, 1.0, -1e100]), sum(...), fsum(...)     [0.0, 1.0, 1.0]
13. reduce(add, [0.1, 0.2, 0.3]), sum(...)                     [0.6000000000000001, 0.6]
14. sum([1, Fraction(1, 3)]), sum([1, 2], 0.0)                 [Fraction(4, 3), 3.0]

No each_with_object: a loop over an outer variable, or a comprehension
15. sizes = {}; for w in words: sizes[w] = len(w)              {'apple': 5, 'banana': 6, 'cherry': 6}
16. reduce(lambda h, w: h | {w: len(w)}, words, {})            {'apple': 5, 'banana': 6, 'cherry': 6}
17. reduce(assign_only, nums, {}) raises                       'TypeError'
18. reduce(lambda acc, x: acc + [x * 10], nums, [])            [10, 20, 30, 40]
19. reduce's function always gets (acc, x)                     [None, ('memo', 5)]
20. acc = []; for w in words: acc.append(w)                    ['apple', 'banana', 'cherry']
21. text = ""; for w in words: text += w  (kept)               'applebananacherry'
22. dict(Counter("banana"))                                    {'b': 1, 'a': 3, 'n': 2}

